# PART 12 — EARTH PROTOTYPE AND CAPSULE DELIVERY: EXACT MANUAL SEQUENCE

This is a critical mission mechanic.

The Earth astronaut must manually complete the entire capsule preparation and delivery process.

Do not automate the whole process with a single button.

### STAGE 1 — COLLECT COMPONENTS

The astronaut visits the inventory room.

They collect the required two or three components.

They place the components into a trolley.

They transport the trolley to the laboratory.

### STAGE 2 — DEVELOP THE PROTOTYPE

Inside the laboratory:

- Remove the components from the trolley.
- Place them on the workbench.
- Assemble the mechanism.
- Connect the required components.
- Complete an appropriate mini-game.
- Produce a small physical prototype or a suitable piece of equipment.

The finished product must be visible in the world.

### STAGE 3 — TEST THE PROTOTYPE

The astronaut carries the prototype to a testing station.

The player activates the test.

The testing process must take AT LEAST 30 SECONDS.

Do not allow instant completion.

During the test:
- Display animated equipment.
- Show progress visually.
- Use lights and small indicators.
- Play suitable machine sounds.
- Show the prototype operating.

After successful testing, mark the prototype as approved.

### STAGE 4 — MANUALLY TRANSPORT THE PROTOTYPE TO THE CAPSULE

The astronaut physically picks up or transports the prototype.

Create a proper connecting corridor or enclosed transfer tunnel between the laboratory and the capsule loading area.

Use the feeling of walking through an aircraft boarding tunnel, but adapted to a space research facility.

The player must physically move through the passage to reach the capsule room.

Do not simply teleport the object or character.

### STAGE 5 — LOAD THE CAPSULE

The capsule must be physically accessible.

The astronaut approaches it and enters the loading area.

The player manually places the prototype inside the capsule.

Show the loading animation.

If multiple pieces of equipment are required, load them individually.

### STAGE 6 — LOCK THE CAPSULE

Once all required equipment is loaded:

- Close the capsule.
- Activate the locking mechanism.
- Show a clear visual confirmation.
- Change the capsule status to READY.

The astronaut must leave the capsule loading area.

### STAGE 7 — RETURN TO THE LAUNCH OBSERVATION AREA

The astronaut physically walks back to the launch control area.

Create a large red launch button near a beautiful glass wall overlooking the launch area.

The launch button must be highly visible and satisfyingly animated.

### STAGE 8 — LAUNCH

The player physically presses the large red launch button.

Play an appropriate confirmation animation and launch sequence.

The capsule launches with its booster.

Use a cinematic camera to show the rocket rising and departing.

### STAGE 9 — MONITORING ROOM

Create a separate monitoring room overlooking the launch area.

The Earth astronaut can view the launch from inside this room.

Show the capsule's progress on large displays.

The player should be able to watch the launch through the glass and also see the mission status on the monitors.

Do not skip this experience.

The capsule delivery process must feel like a real mission milestone.

