Do not create a superficial version of all 20 levels.

Develop the game incrementally while preserving existing functionality.

Build the highest-quality playable foundation possible, then expand it.

Prioritise:

1. Character appearance and animation.
2. Complete UI redesign.
3. Beautiful Mars environment.
4. Excellent dormitory exterior and interior.
5. Proper indoor camera and building navigation.
6. Earth research diversity.
7. Manual prototype and capsule logistics.
8. Building relocation and terrain-aware road construction.
9. Pet behaviour and charging.
10. Random planetary events.
11. Precise planetary navigation.
12. Twenty meaningful levels.

Every feature described must be implemented as actual gameplay where technically possible.

If a feature is not yet implemented, identify it honestly.

Do not pretend a decorative model is an interactive system.

Do not replace functional gameplay with static illustrations.

Do not sacrifice visual quality, animation quality or user experience for unnecessary text.

The player should feel like they are living two connected astronaut lives: discovering science on Earth and building an extraordinary civilisation on Mars.

